In #44778 @mcarilli added a concept of opmath, defined as follows:
// For FP16 or BFloat16 inputs, ops should perform internal math in FP32.
template<typename scalar_t> struct get_opmath_t { using opmath_t = scalar_t; };
template<> struct get_opmath_t<at::Half> { using opmath_t = float; };
template<> struct get_opmath_t<at::BFloat16> { using opmath_t = float; };

This is fairly similar to accscalar_t, but the difference is that integers don't get promoted into int64_t (#44778 (comment)); if we are compute bound, this can matter because 64-bit integer math takes twice as many ops as 32-bit integer math on most CUDA devices.
With #63884 there are no other places where the ability to talk about internal math comes in handy. Thus, I propose that we deify this into a proper concept to be prosletyzed across the whole codebase.
Concretely:

Move the definition to aten/src/ATen/AccumulateType.h or its own header aten/src/ATen/OpMathType.h
Rename the definition for symmetry with AccumulateType; i.e., struct is called OpMathType and then typedef opmath_type = typename OpMathType<T>::type.

